<title>PHILIPPINES: Manila's PHIBOR rates largely softer to steady.</title>
<headline>Manila's PHIBOR rates largely softer to steady.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-02-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Philippine interbank offered rates eased on Wednesday, except for the one-month and six-month maturities which remained steady at 10 1/6 and 10 5/16 percent, respectively.</p>
<p>Traders said swap points between the peso and the dollar generally softened because of ample supply.</p>
<p>&quot;We did not see much play in both sides today because of enough supply of both currencies,&quot; said one trader in a foreign bank.  </p>
<p>Average rates quoted by 20 banks were:</p>
<p>			 FEB 19		  FEB 18</p>
<p>    1 W		9  7/8		  9 15/16</p>
<p>    2 W		9  7/8		  9 15/16</p>
<p>    1 M		10  1/16		10  1/16</p>
<p>    2 M		10  1/16		10  1/8</p>
<p>    3 M		10  1/8		 10  3/16</p>
<p>    6 M		10  5/16		10  5/16</p>
<p>    12M		10  1/2		 10  9/16</p>
<p>    VAL		20-Feb		  19-Feb</p>
<p>-- DOLLY AGLAY (632) 841-89-36, fax 817-62-67</p>
